<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Inference</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Optimized inference accelerate cycle times across multiple tasks with comparable performance (Table <a href="#A5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix E Inference ‣ LeRobot: An Open-Source Library for End-to-End Robot Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), and provide a scalable path to higher model capacity without compromising on real-time control, provided access to a network.
In particular, the speedup presented in Table <a href="#A5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix E Inference ‣ LeRobot: An Open-Source Library for End-to-End Robot Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> derives from <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">logical</em> decoupling—asynchronously computing the next chunk while the current one has not been exhausted yet—rather than physical decoupling, as both the server and client run on the same machine, though in principle the inference stack allows for communication between different machines.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
